Ultravista Academy • Student Manager – Quick Start Guide

I. Launching the App

Double-click the student_manager.py file (or whatever you named it).

The main window opens with a sidebar menu and a student table.



---

II. Viewing Students

View All: Shows the total number of students and the average percentage.

View Individual: Enter a student code to see their full record.

Highest/Lowest Overall: Instantly see the top and bottom performers.



---

III. Searching & Filtering

Type a name or code in the Search box.

Click Clear to remove the filter and see all students again.



---

IV. Adding a Student

1. Click Add Student.


2. A mini-game pops up – press the arrow keys in the correct sequence to unlock the form.


3. Fill in Code, Name, CW1-3, and Exam marks.


4. Click Save. The student is added, stats updated automatically.




---

V. Updating a Student

1. Select a row in the table.


2. Click Update Student (or double-click the row).


3. Complete the mini-game to unlock editing.


4. Edit the fields and click Save.




---

VI. Deleting a Student

1. Select the student in the table.


2. Click Delete Student.


3. Complete the mini-game to confirm deletion.


4. Confirm in the popup.


VII. Sorting Records

Click Sort Records.

Enter asc (ascending) or desc (descending) to sort by overall %.


VIII. Exporting Data

Click Export CSV.

Choose a file location and name.

All student records are exported in a CSV file.


IX. Stats & Cards

Total Students: Number of students loaded.

Average %: Class average.

Top/Lowest Student: Name and code of top/bottom performers.


Tips

Student Codes must be 1000–9999.

CW1–3 marks: 0–20, Exam: 0–100.

Mini-game prevents accidental edits – follow the arrow key prompts.